# coding-agents-kit env file — ~/.config/agentkit/env (mode 600).
# Loaded by `ak` into its own process only, before it starts a CLI. On
# macOS/Linux it is sourced by bash, so shell code works, e.g.
#   XAI_API_KEY="$(security find-generic-password -s xai -w)"
# On Windows only plain KEY=value lines are read.
# Fill keys locally; never paste them into a chat, an issue or a commit.

# --- Permissions: auto (default: every launch adds the CLI's autonomy flag) | ask (opt-out)
# Autonomy is meant for disposable or sandboxed environments; on a host, opt out:
# AGENTKIT_PERMISSIONS=ask

# --- Z.AI GLM (claude-glm, codex-glm, opencode-glm, pi-glm)
# ZAI_CODING_API_KEY=
# ZAI_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL=glm-5.3
# ZAI_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL=glm-5.3
# ZAI_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL=glm-5.3-flash

# --- xAI (codex-xai, opencode-xai, pi-xai, cline-xai, grok)
# XAI_API_KEY=
# XAI_MODEL_DAILY=grok-4.3
# XAI_MODEL_REASONING=grok-4.6

# --- Azure OpenAI / Microsoft Foundry (codex-azure, opencode-azure, pi-azure, cline-azure)
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# AZURE_OPENAI_RESOURCE=          # or AZURE_OPENAI_BASE_URL=
# AZURE_OPENAI_MODEL_DAILY=       # your deployment name (required)
# AZURE_OPENAI_MODEL_REASONING=

# --- A second account: the same variable with the profile's suffix, e.g. for @work
# ZAI_CODING_API_KEY_WORK=
# XAI_API_KEY_2=
